From ef5d0c20afe5f1bb58a0de363dee1e754f1d0951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your_Name <you@example.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:24:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] drm/nouveau/fb/gf100: reclock DDR3 from the VBIOS tables

gf100_ram_calc only knew one GDDR5 board's register values, so Fermi
boards with DDR3 could not change their memory clock. Add a DDR3 path
that follows the NVIDIA driver's sequence and takes its values from the
VBIOS: timings from the v1.0 timing entry, mode registers from
nvkm_sddr3_calc, delay settings from the ramcfg entry, and the memory
PLL from its limits, preferring an exact clock over a higher VCO. The
bits that differ only between the high-speed and the low-speed entries
follow ramcfg_10_02_04; the meaning of most of them is unknown.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 nvkm/subdev/fb/ramgf100.c | 380 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 380 insertions(+)

